],"component-example",{"name":340},"switch-basic",[313,342,343],{"id":301},"Action",[292,345,346,348],{},[295,347,301],{}," runs after toggling, receives the new value and may return a Promise. Use it for settings that are saved through an API as soon as they change, such as enabling an account or notifications.",[338,350],{"name":351},"switch-action",[353,354,355,378],"table",{},[356,357,358],"thead",{},[359,360,361,365,367,372],"tr",{},[362,363,364],"th",{},"Stage",[362,366,152],{},[362,368,369],{},[295,370,371],{},"v-model",[362,373,374,377],{},[295,375,376],{},"change"," event",[379,380,381,396,410,422],"tbody",{},[359,382,383,387,390,393],{},[384,385,386],"td",{},"Pending",[384,388,389],{},"Shows the new value, loading and disabled",[384,391,392],{},"Unchanged",[384,394,395],{},"Not emitted",[359,397,398,401,404,407],{},[384,399,400],{},"Success",[384,402,403],{},"Keeps the new value, loading and disabled end",[384,405,406],{},"Updated to the new value",[384,408,409],{},"Emitted",[359,411,412,415,418,420],{},[384,413,414],{},"Failure",[384,416,417],{},"Goes back to the old value, loading and disabled end",[384,419,392],{},[384,421,395],{},[359,423,424,427,430,432],{},[384,425,426],{},"Error",[384,428,429],{},"Same as failure",[384,431,392],{},[384,433,395],{},[435,436,437,454,471,479],"ul",{},[438,439,440,443,444,447,448,450,451,306],"li",{},[441,442,400],"strong",{},": only returning ",[295,445,446],{},"false"," (or a Promise resolving to ",[295,449,446],{},") counts as a failure. Any other value is a success, including no return value as in ",[295,452,453],{},"async () => { await save(value) }",[438,455,456,459,460,463,464,467,468,470],{},[441,457,458],{},"Errors",": when the action throws, the switch reverts the same way and the error is thrown again, for the global error handler or the console. To notify the user, ",[295,461,462],{},"try","\u002F",[295,465,466],{},"catch"," inside the action, show a message and return ",[295,469,446],{},", as in the example above.",[438,472,473,475,476,478],{},[441,474,386],{},": the switch is disabled, so the action is not called twice. If the page changes ",[295,477,371],{}," while pending, the page's value wins and is not overwritten when the action finishes.",[438,480,481,486,487,489,490,306],{},[441,482,483,484],{},"Without ",[295,485,301],{},", ",[295,488,371],{}," updates right after toggling, the same as ",[295,491,305],{},[292,493,494,495,498,499,502,503,306],{},"The ",[295,496,497],{},"SwitchAction"," and ",[295,500,501],{},"SwitchValue"," types can be imported from ",[295,504,505],{},"#shuo-ui\u002Fcomponents\u002FShuoSwitch.vue",[313,507,509],{"id":508},"on-and-off-values","On and off values",[292,511,512,498,515,518,519,498,522,524,525,463,528,531],{},[295,513,514],{},"true-value",[295,516,517],{},"false-value"," are the bound values when on and off, ",[295,520,521],{},"true",[295,523,446],{}," by default. Change them when the back end uses ",[295,526,527],{},"Y",[295,529,530],{},"N","; the action receives these values too.",[338,533],{"name":534},"switch-values",[313,536,538],{"id":537},"size-and-states","Size and states",[292,540,541,542,545,546,549,550,553,554,557,558,561,562,565,566,569,570,573,574,578],{},"When ",[295,543,544],{},"size"," is not set, it follows the ",[295,547,548],{},"UFormField"," size and the site-wide setting, ",[295,551,552],{},"lg"," built in, the same as the other input components. Without a description, the switch height matches an input of the same size (24 to 40px for ",[295,555,556],{},"xs"," to ",[295,559,560],{},"xl","), so it lines up with other fields in the same row. ",[295,563,564],{},"loading"," shows a loading icon and disables the switch; ",[295,567,568],{},"disabled"," follows the form state when not set; ",[295,571,572],{},"skeleton"," covers it with a skeleton of the same size. See ",[328,575,577],{"href":576},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon","Common props"," for the shared behavior of the states.",[338,580],{"name":